"""MIXFORGE — real Bazel build entry point.

Founder real-time: "ensure we have BAZEL for mixforge." Same real, pragmatic "no external
bazel_dep until something real needs one" precedent PARENA's own MODULE.bazel and MISHRI's own
MODULE.bazel already established -- this repo's own real, hermetic-and-sandboxable piece
(web/dsp_test.mjs, the DSP kernel + rendered-audio test suite) imports nothing beyond Node.js
built-ins plus its own sibling web/engine.mjs and the checked-in web/dsp.wasm, so no
rules_nodejs/aspect_rules_js toolchain is pulled in for it.

Everything else real in this repo -- compiling dsp.wasm itself (needs a sibling ../PARENA build
plus the LLVM/wasm-ld toolchain), the room server (needs `npm install`'s real network access for
the `ws` dependency), and serving web/ for manual browser testing -- is deliberately NOT wrapped
as a hermetic Bazel build/test action. See BUILD.bazel's own doc comments for why each of those
is a `bazel run` convenience wrapper instead.
"""

module(
    name = "mixforge",
    version = "0.1.0",
)

# rules_shell -- Bazel 8+'s own real split: sh_binary/sh_test/sh_library are no longer Starlark
# globals, a real BCR dependency now (same real gotcha MISHRI's own MODULE.bazel already found
# live: "bazel build failed with 'name sh_test is not defined' until this was added").
bazel_dep(name = "rules_shell", version = "0.6.1")
